{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHtfayRXHVch7D7vL7SfLR","type":"tool_result","content":"  1286→## 19. TUI requirements\n  1287→\n  1288→The terminal UI is part of the MVP.\n  1289→\n  1290→## 19.1 Minimum screens\n  1291→\n  1292→1. **Overview**\n  1293→   - day/time\n  1294→   - chemistry summary\n  1295→   - plant summary\n  1296→   - shrimp summary\n  1297→   - event warnings\n  1298→\n  1299→2. **Chemistry**\n  1300→   - temperature\n  1301→   - pH\n  1302→   - DO\n  1303→   - TAN / NH3 / nitrite / nitrate / phosphate\n  1304→   - GH/KH/TDS/conductivity\n  1305→   - trends over recent days\n  1306→\n  1307→3. **Biology**\n  1308→   - plants\n  1309→   - algae/periphyton\n  1310→   - shrimp population\n  1311→   - reproduction\n  1312→   - hidden-state summaries like biofilter maturity and microfauna health\n  1313→\n  1314→4. **Actions**\n  1315→   - feed\n  1316→   - water change\n  1317→   - trim\n  1318→   - siphon\n  1319→   - change ambient temp\n  1320→   - change light / heater settings\n  1321→\n  1322→5. **Event log**\n  1323→   - chronological causal log\n  1324→\n  1325→## 19.2 Time controls\n  1326→\n  1327→- advance 1 hour\n  1328→- advance 1 day\n  1329→- advance 1 week\n  1330→- pause/autoadvance\n  1331→\n  1332→---\n  1333→\n  1334→## 20. Acceptance tests and regression scenarios\n  1335→\n  1336→These are mandatory.\n  1337→\n  1338→## 20.1 Determinism test\n  1339→Given identical seed and action sequence, snapshots must match exactly or within fixed float tolerance.\n  1340→\n  1341→## 20.2 Mass balance test\n  1342→Water change removes the expected fraction of dissolved constituents.\n  1343→\n  1344→## 20.3 Tank-size stability test\n  1345→With identical feed mass and livestock addition:\n  1346→- 10 L tank must show larger concentration swings than 100 L tank\n  1347→- 10 L tank must change temperature faster after ambient temp jump\n  1348→\n  1349→## 20.4 Ambient temperature test\n  1350→Scenario:\n  1351→- stable tank at 24 °C\n  1352→- ambient raised to 31 °C\n  1353→Expected:\n  1354→- water warms over time, not instantly\n  1355→- DO saturation target falls\n  1356→- shrimp stress rises if sustained\n  1357→- heater usage drops to zero if heater present\n  1358→\n  1359→## 20.5 Cycling test\n  1360→Brand-new tanks with identical setup but different seeded states should show different time-to-stability.\n  1361→\n  1362→Expected:\n  1363→- TAN and nitrite do not disappear instantly\n  1364→- nitrifier biomass grows over time\n  1365→- filter cleaning early in the cycle can delay maturation\n  1366→\n  1367→## 20.6 Overfeeding test\n  1368→Repeated overfeeding must produce:\n  1369→- rising detritus\n  1370→- increased oxygen demand\n  1371→- TAN increase\n  1372→- elevated algae risk\n  1373→\n  1374→## 20.7 Rooted substrate test\n  1375→A rooted plant guild in nutrient-rich substrate must outperform the same guild in inert sand under otherwise equal conditions.\n  1376→\n  1377→## 20.8 Reproduction thermal stress test\n  1378→At high sustained temperature, shrimp reproduction readiness and success must fall relative to moderate temperature conditions.\n  1379→\n  1380→## 20.9 Water change chemistry shock test\n  1381→A large water change with very different GH/KH/TDS must improve some waste metrics while potentially increasing stress.\n  1382→\n  1383→---\n  1384→\n  1385→## 21. Milestone plan for an implementation agent\n  1386→\n  1387→## Milestone 0 — repository skeleton\n  1388→Deliver:\n  1389→- cargo workspace\n  1390→- core types\n  1391→- build/test CI\n  1392→- sample config loading\n  1393→- save/load roundtrip test\n  1394→\n  1395→## Milestone 1 — tank geometry and temperature\n  1396→Deliver:\n  1397→- `TankGeometry`\n  1398→- `EnvironmentState`\n  1399→- `HardwareState`\n  1400→- temperature update system\n  1401→- ambient temperature action\n  1402→- heater logic\n  1403→- tank-size comparison tests\n  1404→\n  1405→## Milestone 2 — dissolved pools and water changes\n  1406→Deliver:\n  1407→- `WaterState`\n  1408→- source water profiles\n  1409→- water change/top-off actions\n  1410→- TDS / GH / KH / conductivity derivation\n  1411→- chemistry snapshot rendering\n  1412→\n  1413→## Milestone 3 — nitrogen + oxygen cycle\n  1414→Deliver:\n  1415→- detritus pools\n  1416→- decomposition\n  1417→- nitrification guilds\n  1418→- oxygen dynamics\n  1419→- NH3 fraction calculation\n  1420→- event warnings\n  1421→\n  1422→## Milestone 4 — substrate + plants + algae\n  1423→Deliver:\n  1424→- substrate layers\n  1425→- plant guilds\n  1426→- algae/periphyton\n  1427→- light schedule\n  1428→- rooted vs water-column nutrient access\n  1429→- trim action\n  1430→\n  1431→## Milestone 5 — shrimp + microfauna\n  1432→Deliver:\n  1433→- shrimp population model\n  1434→- food-web linkage to biofilm/periphyton\n  1435→- reproduction / molt stress\n  1436→- high-temperature reproduction penalty\n  1437→- microfauna abstraction\n  1438→\n  1439→## Milestone 6 — TUI MVP\n  1440→Deliver:\n  1441→- overview/chemistry/biology/actions/log screens\n  1442→- time controls\n  1443→- scenario selection\n  1444→- save/load support\n  1445→\n  1446→## Milestone 7 — validation + balancing\n  1447→Deliver:\n  1448→- regression scenarios\n  1449→- parameter audit with provenance\n  1450→- balancing pass for plausible trajectories\n  1451→- documentation of known simplifications\n  1452→\n  1453→---\n  1454→\n  1455→## 22. Initial parameter packs required\n  1456→\n  1457→The first data pack must include:\n  1458→\n  1459→### Source water profile presets\n  1460→- soft acidic\n  1461→- moderate community-tank water\n  1462→- hard alkaline shrimp water\n  1463→- RO-like low-mineral water\n  1464→\n  1465→### Substrate presets\n  1466→- inert sand\n  1467→- inert gravel\n  1468→- active planted substrate\n  1469→- coarse porous media mix\n  1470→\n  1471→### Plant guild presets\n  1472→- fast stem\n  1473→- rooted rosette\n  1474→- moss/epiphyte\n  1475→- floating plant (optional v1.1)\n  1476→\n  1477→### Shrimp pack\n  1478→- `Neocaridina davidi`\n  1479→  - moderate temperature optimum\n  1480→  - high-temp reproductive penalty\n  1481→  - biofilm grazing preference\n  1482→  - GH dependence proxy\n  1483→  - moderate juvenile sensitivity\n  1484→\n  1485→---"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013yHGd5uFJHJgdiXSiSjdyf","session_id":"5afc8472-1402-44b3-9d7c-1a241eb51364","uuid":"61b33374-277e-4322-808a-6eb458a93610"}
