{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013yHGd5uFJHJgdiXSiSjdyf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive final report.\n\n---\n\n## Tank Simulation TUI - Comprehensive Verification Report\n\n### 1. REQUIRED SCREENS - ALL PRESENT ✓\n\nAll five required screens are implemented with proper rendering code:\n\n**Located at:** `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/`\n\n- **Overview** (`overview.rs`) - Renders:\n  - Day/time display\n  - Water column chemistry (temp, pH, DO, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate)\n  - Hardware status (volume, DIC, GH, KH, TDS, light, heater, aeration)\n  - Plant status (total biomass, fast stem, rosette health indices)\n  - Shrimp status (adults, juveniles, berried, condition, molt stress, reproduction)\n  - Active warnings list\n\n- **Chemistry** (`chemistry.rs`) - Renders:\n  - Dissolved chemistry (pH, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC)\n  - Derived values (DO, GH, KH, TDS, conductivity, temperature)\n  - Historical trends with sparklines for pH, TAN, DO, temperature with directional arrows\n\n- **Biology** (`biology.rs`) - Renders:\n  - Plant guilds (fast stem, root rosette biomass and health, substrate nutrients)\n  - Algae/detritus (suspended algae, periphyton, nuisance index, detritus pools)\n  - Shrimp population (counts by stage, condition, molt stress, readiness)\n  - Biofilter maturity (AOB, NOB, comammox, decomposer biomass)\n  - Microfauna summary (population index, grazing pressure, filter cleanliness)\n\n- **Actions** (`actions.rs`) - Action form system with 12 action types\n\n- **Log** (`log.rs`) - Renders:\n  - Recent events chronologically\n  - Event severity color-coding (info/warning/critical)\n  - Event kind, day, hour, summary, and cause codes\n\n---\n\n### 2. REQUIRED CONTROLS - ALL PRESENT ✓\n\n**Time controls** (implemented in `input.rs` and `lib.rs`):\n- `h` - Step 1 hour ✓\n- `d` - Step 1 day (24 hours) ✓\n- `w` - Step 1 week (168 hours) ✓\n- `space` - Toggle auto-advance/pause ✓\n\n**Navigation controls** (implemented in `input.rs` and `lib.rs`):\n- `Tab` - Cycle next screen ✓\n- `1-5` - Jump to specific screen (Overview, Chemistry, Biology, Actions, Log) ✓\n- `q` - Quit ✓\n\n**Save/Load controls** (implemented in `input.rs` and `lib.rs`):\n- `s` - Save to disk (calls `save_to_disk()` which serializes engine state to JSON) ✓\n- `l` - Load from disk (calls `load_from_disk()` which deserializes SaveFile and rebuilds engine) ✓\n\n**Actions screen controls** (implemented in `input.rs`):\n- `Up/Down` - Navigate between actions\n- `Left/Right` - Navigate between fields\n- `[/]` - Cycle choice fields (source water selection)\n- `t` - Toggle boolean fields (aeration enabled)\n- `Backspace` - Delete from numeric field\n- `0-9 and .` - Edit numeric fields\n- `Enter` - Submit action\n\n---\n\n### 3. STATE MANAGEMENT - CLEAN ARCHITECTURE ✓\n\n**TUI uses ONLY TankSnapshot and PlayerAction dispatch - verified:**\n\nLocated in: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/lib.rs`\n\n- **Engine encapsulation**: Core state stored in `self.engine: Engine`\n- **Snapshot-based rendering**: All screens read from `&app.snapshot: TankSnapshot` (immutable borrows)\n- **Action dispatch**: `app.apply_action(action: PlayerAction)` is the only path to state mutation\n- **No direct mutation**: All screen rendering code uses `let snapshot = &app.snapshot` (read-only)\n\n**Verified patterns:**\n- `apply_action()` → calls `self.engine.apply_action()` → calls `refresh_snapshot()`\n- `step_hours()` → calls `self.engine.step_hours()` → calls `refresh_snapshot()`\n- `refresh_snapshot()` → creates new snapshot from engine state\n- Snapshot history maintained for trends (sparkline data)\n- Save/load preserves engine state via `SaveFile` serialization\n\n---\n\n### 4. ACTIONS SCREEN FORMS - ALL REQUIRED FORMS PRESENT ✓\n\n**ActionKind enum** (12 actions, all implemented with form fields):\n\nLocated in: `/root/